        "NC_GLOBAL": {
          "featureType": "timeSeries",
          "title": "FRF 11m AWAC Waves",
          "station_name": "11m-AWAC",
          "summary": "USACE/COAB data collected by a bottom mounted (looking up) Nortek AWAC, approximately 1150m offshore  of Duck (FRF), NC at a nominal depth of 11m NAVD88.  Directional spectra are computed using a custom  COAB analysis of merging low frequency AST-UV (or PUV) spectra with high-end beam-array spectra  (see http link frf.usace.army.mil/realtime/awac/COAB_awacSpectralAnalysis.pdf).  Data collection is  hard-wired and analyzed hourly with 34 minute timeseries records.  Two dimensional frequency-direction  spectra are computed using a Maximum Likelihood Estimator (MLE) method.  The Fourier coefficients  were estimated from the 2D spectra.  A description of computing these coefficients is provided in Use of advanced directional wave spectra analysis methods, M. D. Earle, K. E. Steele, and D. W. C. Wang,  Ocean Engineering, Volume 26, Issue 12, December 1999, Pages 1421-1434. Or Kuik et. al, JPO, 18,  pp. 1020-1034, 1988.\n",
